Patchlevel 9 has just been installed at my site. Unfortunately it keeps
stopping itself whenever the <ctrl>y command is entered. I am used to using
the control (direction) commands to move around, so this is somewhat
inconvenient. Is this a general bug in the code, or is it perhaps the result
of a faulty installation peculiar to this site.

When the <ctrl>y command is used, the cursor moves to the left and the 
message `% Stopped' is printed. When processes are listed the process
nethack has condition `T'. This is very annoying since it is impossible for 
me to restart this process or kill it directly (it says I am not the owner),
nor can I log out normally with stopped jobs. If I try to run the nethack
program it tells me I have a game already in progress.  Each time this happens
I must log myself out by manually killing my root process, log myself back in
again, and then restart nethack. Luckily it always saves my game, however
going through this rigmarole every five minutes sure takes a lot of the fun
out of playing.

